Striking the right balance between promoting digital safety and preserving access to innovative, valuable digital services requires a more nuanced regulatory framework. Such a framework could be built on the following pillars:
1. All digital providers would be subject to baseline management responsibilities to design and operate their services in a way that mitigates digital safety risks, based on accepted standards2 that are tailored to the specific attributes of their services;
2. These management responsibilities would generate variation among types of services, where some digital services with attributes that pose greater risks of harm would be subject to heightened responsibilities;

